 the cross-level events. Cross-level conditions must be modified to check against appropriate tables (up and down) to trigger the correct trade actions based on the specified algorithm.  The logic for detecting a level cross should check for crosses through `fractalsUp` and `fractalsDown`, and the trade condition should update to reflect the \"long\" (BUY) on the down-to-up break and \"short\" (SELL) on the up-to-down break.\n\n```lua\nfunction LevelCross()\n    if prevPrice == 0 then return end\n\n    virt = VirtualPos()\n\n    if not opn and not virt and count_t == 0 and count_v == 0 then\n        startPrice = 0\n    end\n\n    -- Check for crosses in fractalsDown (support)\n    for i = 1, #fractalsDown do\n        local f = fractalsDown[i]\n        local crossDownUp = (prevPrice > f and currentPrice <= f)\n\n        if crossDownUp then\n            -- Open Long trade\n            Trade()\n        end\n    end\n\n    -- Check for crosses in fractalsUp (resistance)\n    for i = 1, #fractalsUp do\n        local f = fractalsUp[i]\n        local crossUpDown = (prevPrice < f and currentPrice >= f)\n\n        if crossUpDown then\n            -- Open Short trade\n            OpenVirt()\n        end\n    end\nend\n```\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"& \"C:\\Program Files\\Git\\cmd\\git.exe\" -C \"Y:\\my_fractal\" log -n 5","Cwd":"Y:\\my_fractal","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Checking git log of my_fractal","toolSummary":"Check commit history of my_fractal repo"}}]}
